<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Halabja massacre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1988">1988</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Halabja chemical attack</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Halabja massacre was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chemical-weapons">chemical weapons</a> attack by Iraqi forces on the Kurdish town of Halabja on 16 March 1988, near the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran-iraq-war">Iran–Iraq War</a>. Mustard gas and nerve agents killed an estimated 3,200 to 5,000 people, most of them civilians, and injured thousands more. It is the deadliest chemical attack on a civilian population in history, and an Iraqi court recognised it as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> in 2010.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/halabja-massacre.jpg" alt="Halabja massacre" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mehdi Jamshidi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Omer_Khawar_and_his_infant_by_Mehdi_Jamshidi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
